backfire is an independent, from-scratch implementation. Its architecture — a
single binary that runs either the exposed or the origin half of a reverse
tunnel, driven by an interactive menu and per-tunnel systemd units — was
inspired by the design of the BackPack project (https://github.com/AminMGMT/BackPack).
No source code was copied from that project; backfire shares none of its code
and carries its own license.

Third-party libraries (each under its own permissive license):
